{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788979491,"nonce":"HCWETD/DRq1IK4sf9E64CrKIGWM=","message":"Fixed in 39aad6d, and the shape was different from what this issue described.\n\nbuild.rs already warned about embedding a DEBUG cdylib into a release build. The real defect was staleness with no profile mismatch at all: candidates were tried in a fixed order and the FIRST existing one won, so a leftover in \u003ctarget-dir\u003e/\u003ctriple\u003e/\u003cprofile\u003e/ was preferred over a freshly built one in \u003ctarget-dir\u003e/\u003cprofile\u003e/ indefinitely. That is what fed game.hl a runtime with no hlp_alloc_obj_sized.\n\nTwo changes. Within a profile the newest candidate now wins, with the requested profile still beating a newer build of the other. And because nothing here rebuilds the cdylib, an embedded runtime older than std/src now warns.\n\nCaught live while testing: the check fired on this tree, where a Sep 7 triple-qualified dylib was being preferred over a Sep 9 one.","files":null}]}